      "etymology_chain": [
              {
                      "relationship": "Inherited from",
                      "language": "Arabic",
                      "term": "ذَا",
                      "definition": "this (masculine singular demonstrative base with analogical -n)"
              },
              {
                      "relationship": "From",
                      "language": "Classical Arabic",
                      "term": "ذَا",
                      "definition": "masculine proximal demonstrative root"
              }
      ],
      "etymology_notes": "Inherited from Arabic masculine demonstrative base ذَا (ḏā). While earlier 20th-century philologists (Aquilina 1973: 16) compared final -n to ancient Semitic forms (Biblical Aramaic dēn, Phoenician zn) to refute Barbera's Sicilian borrowing theory, modern comparative Maltese and Arabic linguistics (Borg, Vanhove) refutes any ancient substrate origin. Instead, final -n is analyzed as an internal dialectal Arabic innovation: the plural nasal from dawn (cp. Maghrebi hadun / hadhūna) spread analogically to the singulars (da > dan, di > din), reinforced by the proximal locative hawn ('here'). The bare stem survives in proclitic da, while the Classical/MSA compound with deictic hā- (هٰذَا hāḏā) survives in oratorical hedan via Maltese imāla (hā- > he-).",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text_en": "this; used as a determiner to identify a specific singular masculine person, object, or entity nearby in space, present in time, or previously mentioned",
          "text_mt": "Determinant dimostrattiv maskil użat ma' nom definit biex jindika persuna, oġġett jew entità fil-qrib fl-ispazju, preżenti fil-ħin, jew li għadha kif issemmiet.",
          "register": "standard",
          "nuance": "determiner (attributive)"
        },
        {
          "text_en": "used as a pronoun to refer to a specific masculine person, thing, fact, or situation close at hand, currently experienced, or just stated",
          "text_mt": "Pronom dimostrattiv użat bħala suġġett jew oġġett biex jirreferi għal persuna, ħaġa, ġrajja jew sitwazzjoni konkreta jew astratta li tinsab fil-qrib jew li għadha kif ġiet ippreżentata.",
          "register": "standard",
          "nuance": "pronoun (substantive)"
        },
        {
          "text_en": "indicating the current, ongoing, or immediately upcoming period of time",
          "text_mt": "Jindika l-perjodu ta' żmien kurrenti, kontinwu jew li ġej minnufih (eż. dan il-lejl, dan ix-xahar, dan is-sajf, daż-żmien).",
          "register": "standard",
          "nuance": "temporal reference"
        }
      ],
      "usage_examples": [
        {
          "mt": "Dan il-ktieb fih tagħrif siewi ħafna dwar l-istorja ta' Malta.",
          "en": "This book contains very useful information about the history of Malta."
        },
        {
          "mt": "Dan mhuwiex dak li ftehemna dwaru fil-laqgħa tal-bieraħ.",
          "en": "This is not what we agreed upon in yesterday's meeting."
        },
        {
          "mt": "Se norganizzaw seminar nazzjonali dan ix-xahar.",
          "en": "We are organizing a national seminar this month."
        }
      ],
